---
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
---

<SiteLayout title="Projects | Productive Superintelligence">
    <section class="page-section" aria-labelledby="projects-title">
        <p class="label">Projects</p>
        <h1 id="projects-title">Flagship frameworks.</h1>
        <hr />
        <p class="section-copy">
            LLLM, SSSN, and AAAX are the flagship PSI framework trio. Each keeps
            one center abstraction, one implementation layer, and one service
            surface so systems can stay small alone and compose uniformly as
            servers.
        </p>
        <p class="section-copy muted">
            One framework, one abstraction, one layer. Shared structure makes
            Tactics, Channels, and Shells packageable, inspectable, and callable
            through the same PSI service grammar.
        </p>

        <div class="package-grid">
            <a href="https://lllm.one" class="package-block">
                <span class="package-desc">Tactic framework / Runtime layer</span>
                <img src="/lllm-logo-text-dark.png" alt="lllm" class="package-logo" />
            </a>
            <a href="https://sssn.one" class="package-block">
                <span class="package-desc">Channel framework / Backend layer</span>
                <img src="/sssn-logo-text-dark.png" alt="sssn" class="package-logo" />
            </a>
            <a href="https://aaax.one" class="package-block">
                <span class="package-desc">Strategy framework / Shell layer</span>
                <img src="/aaax-logo-text-dark.png" alt="aaax" class="package-logo" />
            </a>
        </div>

        <div class="page-list">
            <a href="https://lllm.one">
                <span class="item-title">LLLM: Tactic + Runtime</span>
                <span class="item-copy">A Tactic is the reusable unit of agentic work. Runtime adapters make Python, Pydantic AI, native LLLM, and future runtimes share one callable service surface.</span>
            </a>
            <a href="https://sssn.one">
                <span class="item-title">SSSN: Channel + Backend</span>
                <span class="item-copy">A Channel is the semantic data contract. Backend implementations provide local stores, HTTP services, remote clients, and future data systems behind the same abstraction.</span>
            </a>
            <a href="https://aaax.one">
                <span class="item-title">AAAX: Strategy + Shell</span>
                <span class="item-copy">A Strategy names mounted package resources. Shell surfaces expose that strategy as a CLI for humans, FastAPI for apps, and agentic context for Codex or Claude Code.</span>
            </a>
        </div>
    </section>
</SiteLayout>
